From 80fcb6a291ec534ece25910c18a1fc939a7790a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kyle Havlovitz <kylehav@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:46:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] Support optional Pokemon Stadium transformations

Run the source-owned transformation scheduler and collision actors when the
match config enables stadium_transformations; preserve frozen defaults.
Extract and share the four transformation archives, prewarm actor pools and
reserve dynamic collision islands before sealing each enabled match.

Correct the source transition timer and slope-IK pose cache invalidation
exposed by rock-form recordings. Export live collision geometry for viewers.
Add six replay fixtures covering all four forms, compare recorded stage phases
and types, and exercise mode-changing resets, copy/save/restore and allocation
bounds across 80,000 frames.

Validation: native and release gates pass 518 replays / 4,771,887 frames;
146 CI-selected Python tests pass. Fresh extraction is deterministic. The
existing scalar last-stock smoke assertion also fails on untouched fcc46464;
the remaining native smoke executables pass separately.

Five alternating release benchmark pairs against fcc46464 show no measurable
frozen-path regression: median 123,370 -> 123,840 FPS at batch 256 and
120,306 -> 120,759 at 512, with identical output digests. Default per-env
storage is unchanged; enabled Fox matches add 2,112 arena bytes and shared
immutable arenas add 1,238,048 bytes per process. Measurements are retained
in agent_docs/performance/BASELINE.md.

(cherry picked from upstream commit b1192b5fbd02a400f6aa91c019de07b0fd10b2cc onto visual-only/04-shake)

Combined with this branch: the setting is packed as #45 packs the arithmetic
flags, in an existing config byte (slippi_patches bit 1,
MSL_PATCH_STADIUM_TRANSFORMATIONS, read through
msl_core_config_stadium_transformations), so MslCoreMatchConfig stays 64 bytes
and the benchmark tape stays version 5 (export cache version 7); the public
MslMatchConfig keeps upstream's stadium_transformations byte. The transition's
jumbotron step (grStadium_801D4548 case 2) calls grStadium_801D2528 hosted, as
#60's display schedule does elsewhere. Suite counts are this branch's plus the
six Stadium fixtures. The viewer schema exports slippiPatches.

